<script>window.BIKES = {{ bikes | dump | safe }};</script>
<div class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-hero__content">
      <span class="category-tag">Tools</span>
      <h1>Gear Ratio &amp; Sprocket Calculator</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lead">Calculate top speed per gear, see how sprocket swaps change your bike's performance, and dial in your gearing before you buy.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="calc-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="calc-layout">

      <div class="calc-intro">
        <p>Sprocket swaps are one of the cheapest and most effective modifications you can make to a motorcycle. Going up one tooth on the rear sprocket softens acceleration and raises top speed; going down one tooth sharpens it. This motorcycle gear ratio calculator lets you model any sprocket combination and immediately see the effect on estimated top speed in every gear — before you spend a cent.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="calc-card">
        <h2 class="calc-card__title">Select Your Bike (Optional)</h2>
        <div class="calc-grid" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="make-select">Make</label>
            <select id="make-select"><option value="">-- Select Make --</option></select>
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="model-select">Model</label>
            <select id="model-select" disabled><option value="">-- Select Model --</option></select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h2 class="calc-card__title">Sprocket &amp; Tyre Setup</h2>
        <div class="calc-grid">
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="front-sprocket">Front Sprocket (teeth)</label>
            <input type="number" id="front-sprocket" value="15" min="10" max="25" step="1">
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="rear-sprocket">Rear Sprocket (teeth)</label>
            <input type="number" id="rear-sprocket" value="42" min="25" max="60" step="1">
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="tire-width">Tyre Width (mm)</label>
            <select id="tire-width">
              <option value="120">120</option>
              <option value="150">150</option>
              <option value="160" selected>160</option>
              <option value="170">170</option>
              <option value="180">180</option>
              <option value="190">190</option>
              <option value="200">200</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="aspect-ratio">Aspect Ratio</label>
            <select id="aspect-ratio">
              <option value="50">50</option>
              <option value="55">55</option>
              <option value="60" selected>60</option>
              <option value="65">65</option>
              <option value="70">70</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="wheel-size">Wheel Size (in)</label>
            <select id="wheel-size">
              <option value="17" selected>17"</option>
              <option value="18">18"</option>
              <option value="19">19"</option>
              <option value="21">21"</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field">
            <label for="max-rpm">Max RPM</label>
            <input type="number" id="max-rpm" value="10000" min="5000" max="15000" step="500">
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="calc-card__title" style="margin-top:2rem;">Gear Ratios</h2>
        <div class="calc-field" style="max-width:200px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
          <label for="gear-count">Number of Gears</label>
          <select id="gear-count">
            <option value="4">4</option>
            <option value="5">5</option>
            <option value="6" selected>6</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="gear-ratios-grid" id="gear-ratios-grid">
          <div class="calc-field gear-row" data-gear="1">
            <label>Gear 1</label>
            <input type="number" id="gr-1" value="2.846" min="0.5" max="5" step="0.001">
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field gear-row" data-gear="2">
            <label>Gear 2</label>
            <input type="number" id="gr-2" value="2.062" min="0.5" max="5" step="0.001">
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field gear-row" data-gear="3">
            <label>Gear 3</label>
            <input type="number" id="gr-3" value="1.647" min="0.5" max="5" step="0.001">
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field gear-row" data-gear="4">
            <label>Gear 4</label>
            <input type="number" id="gr-4" value="1.368" min="0.5" max="5" step="0.001">
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field gear-row" data-gear="5">
            <label>Gear 5</label>
            <input type="number" id="gr-5" value="1.190" min="0.5" max="5" step="0.001">
          </div>
          <div class="calc-field gear-row" data-gear="6">
            <label>Gear 6</label>
            <input type="number" id="gr-6" value="1.037" min="0.5" max="5" step="0.001">
          </div>
        </div>

        <button class="calc-btn" id="calc-btn" onclick="calculate()">Calculate</button>
      </div>

      <div class="calc-results" id="calc-results" style="display:none;">
        <h2 class="calc-card__title">Results</h2>

        <div class="result-summary" id="result-summary"></div>

        <h3 class="results-subtitle">Speed Per Gear at Max RPM</h3>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="results-table" id="results-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Gear</th>
                <th>Gear Ratio</th>
                <th>Speed (km/h)</th>
                <th>Speed (mph)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="results-tbody"></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="results-subtitle">Sprocket Swap Preview</h3>
        <p class="swap-note">Effect of changing one tooth on your current setup:</p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="results-table" id="swap-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Change</th>
                <th>Overall Ratio</th>
                <th>Top Speed (km/h)</th>
                <th>Top Speed (mph)</th>
                <th>vs Stock</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="swap-tbody"></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="seo-section">
        <h2>About This Motorcycle Gear Ratio Calculator</h2>
        <p>This motorcycle gear ratio calculator helps riders understand how gearing changes translate to real-world speed. Enter your sprocket sizes, tyre profile, and gear ratios to instantly see your estimated top speed in every gear. Whether you're planning a sprocket swap or just curious about your bike's gearing, this tool gives you the numbers before you commit.</p>

        <h2>What Is Gear Ratio?</h2>
        <p>The overall gear ratio of a motorcycle is determined by dividing the rear sprocket teeth by the front sprocket teeth. A higher number means more torque multiplication and stronger acceleration; a lower number means higher top speed at the cost of low-end pull. The final-drive ratio combines with each gearbox ratio to give a unique drive ratio for every gear.</p>

        <h2>How Sprocket Changes Affect Speed</h2>
        <p>Adding one tooth to the rear sprocket (or removing one from the front) lowers your overall ratio, increasing acceleration but reducing top speed by a small percentage. Removing a rear tooth does the opposite — top speed increases slightly but the bike feels lazier off the line. Small changes have a surprisingly noticeable effect, especially in lower gears.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

